## TODO: search-state-persistence

When a user opens a mod from the Browse page and navigates back (back arrow or ESC),
they are returned to the initial Browse page state instead of their previous search results.
Sort selection (e.g. "updated date") also resets on each visit.

Root cause: `BrowsePage` unmounts on tab switch (intentional, for fresh data), which discards
all local search/sort/scroll state. Fix would require lifting search state up to `App.tsx`
or preserving it with CSS-hidden approach (same as `InstalledPage` / `SettingsPage`).

Note: the fresh-fetch-on-visit behavior is desirable - only the search/sort *inputs* need
to survive navigation, not the results themselves.

