## TODO: manifest-backfill-and-size

Phase 3, after pak-entries-schema ships. Trigger the manifest backfill run in GitHub
Actions (plain backfill - the missing-manifest set drives it), then measure the real
index.db size increase. Estimate is +8-12 MB over the current ~17.6 MB, paid by every
app user on the 1-hour TTL download. Decision was deliberately deferred until the
number is real. Options, in order of preference if it is too heavy:

1. Keep as is (if the real number is modest)
2. Dedupe entry paths into a separate paths table with a junction (popular assets are
   overridden by many mods, so paths repeat heavily and this compresses well)
3. Move manifests to a third release asset the app fetches lazily (only when a UE-game
   conflict check actually needs it)

